Code Red: payload moves (owner, 2026-10-09: bytes are the universal medium). A move may make bytes
instead of answering: ERROR makes a sound, FLASH a picture. The page judges the bytes and, on a hit,
drops them into the payload mailbox (4156 B, version 2: header, 16-color palette, wave header, 4096 bytes) in GBA
form (≤ 4096 signed 8 kHz samples / ≤ 4 frames of 4bpp tiles); when the battle takes the hit, the GBA plays the sound once through
the cry player (~0.5 s) or animates a 32×32 sprite over the target at 2×. The hook lives in patch 006
(CodeRedMoveContinue → CodeRedPayloadShow). The mailbox is heap-allocated for the battle's duration
(AllocateBattleResources / FreeBattleResources); the static symbol gCodeRedPayload is a pointer to it,
NULL outside battle, so hosts read the pointer first.
